WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.211
- Previously on The O.C.:
- Are we doing this?

00:00:02.461 --> 00:00:04.589
It's not like we haven't before.

00:00:04.798 --> 00:00:08.052
You can't drink, you can't have sushi.
What are you, pregnant?

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.306
One of our partners went behind
our backs to a friend at city council...

00:00:11.514 --> 00:00:13.350
...and got them to deny us
the liquor license.

00:00:13.559 --> 00:00:16.103
So he's profiting from our loss.
He's Caleb Nichol.

00:00:16.312 --> 00:00:18.023
You're upset because
she's marrying Dad.

00:00:18.231 --> 00:00:19.232
Yeah, for his money.

00:00:19.441 --> 00:00:22.278
Last time I talked to Marissa,
she was planning on moving in with us.

00:00:23.696 --> 00:00:25.824
Manipulate me?!
Hold my daughter hostage?!

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:27.242
Theresa's pregnant.

00:00:27.451 --> 00:00:29.036
And it might not be Eddie's.

00:00:37.964 --> 00:00:40.384
Thor. It's a strong name.

00:00:41.135 --> 00:00:43.805
- No one's gonna mess with Thor.
- Thanks.

00:00:44.013 --> 00:00:46.183
Seth's a good name for a boy too.

00:00:46.391 --> 00:00:49.312
Although, at Camp Tokaho,
I was often referred to as a girl...

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.106
...so I guess it works either way.

00:00:51.314 --> 00:00:54.652
- Can we not play the name game?
- Right. Sorry. It's premature.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:56.404
She's probably not even pregnant.

00:00:56.612 --> 00:00:58.698
- Maybe you shoot blanks.
- I feel much better.

00:00:59.116 --> 00:01:02.578
Sorry. If you're in no mood to kid,
l..."Kid."

00:01:02.787 --> 00:01:04.622
That's an unfortunate choice of a word.

00:01:04.956 --> 00:01:08.586
- We don't even know if this kid is mine.
- We don't even know if there is a kid.

00:01:08.794 --> 00:01:10.880
How much faith can you put
in a pee swab?

00:01:11.089 --> 00:01:12.340
Seth, don't say "swab."

00:01:12.549 --> 00:01:14.718
Ryan Atwood just made a joke.

00:01:14.927 --> 00:01:16.971
Yeah. Gotta keep
a sense of humor, right?

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:21.227
Hey, stuffed in a locker, shoes full
of the water-polo team's urine...

00:01:21.435 --> 00:01:22.979
...never funnier.
- Good to know.

00:01:23.187 --> 00:01:25.398
Yeah. In fact, having you around
to defend me...

00:01:25.607 --> 00:01:28.360
...I've kind of gotten soft
not having anyone picking on me.

00:01:28.527 --> 00:01:32.741
So really been no need
for the Seth Cohen retaliatory zinger.

00:01:41.961 --> 00:01:44.547
My dad hates cilantro.
If you put cilantro on anything...

00:01:44.756 --> 00:01:46.633
...I may be uninvited to the wedding.

00:01:46.842 --> 00:01:48.511
Somebody get me some cilantro.

00:01:48.719 --> 00:01:51.389
Colored lights? No way.
White lights only...

00:01:51.598 --> 00:01:55.394
...because colored lights remind my father
of a carnival, and he hates carnies.

00:01:55.603 --> 00:01:58.607
Note to self: Hang with carnies.

00:01:59.316 --> 00:02:00.859
Yeah. Great.

00:02:01.026 --> 00:02:04.489
I'll see you on Saturday. Thanks. Bye.

00:02:06.575 --> 00:02:08.744
Well, the wedding rehearsal is confirmed.

00:02:09.412 --> 00:02:11.247
This wedding is actually happening.

00:02:11.456 --> 00:02:13.417
Never have people deserved
each other more.

00:02:13.625 --> 00:02:15.920
I can't believe my dad is
walking with a black eye.

00:02:16.128 --> 00:02:18.590
I know. That's because
Jimmy punched him.

00:02:18.798 --> 00:02:20.884
If I had, he'd be walking
with a broken nose.

00:02:21.093 --> 00:02:23.262
What are the odds of you
making up before the wedding?

00:02:23.471 --> 00:02:26.224
I would say not good at all.

00:02:26.433 --> 00:02:28.227
It's important to me.

00:02:28.436 --> 00:02:31.398
A daughter wants her father to be happy
on his wedding day.

00:02:31.606 --> 00:02:35.653
And here I was thinking it was
supposed to be the other way around.

00:02:38.448 --> 00:02:40.868
Well, what if I...

00:02:41.076 --> 00:02:43.121
...begged?

00:02:44.372 --> 00:02:45.957
Groveled?

00:02:46.124 --> 00:02:48.252
- Maybe cajoled?
- Oh, honey, come on.

00:02:48.461 --> 00:02:49.837
He sabotaged my restaurant.

00:02:50.004 --> 00:02:54.969
He committed fraud. There's no way
I could possibly forgive him.

00:03:02.562 --> 00:03:05.649
Well, maybe I could pretend...

00:03:05.982 --> 00:03:07.902
...to forgive him.

00:03:14.743 --> 00:03:20.167
Maybe I could apologize
with my fingers crossed.

00:03:25.632 --> 00:03:27.468
Hey, you're not at school.

00:03:27.676 --> 00:03:29.428
Yeah, we were at the doctor's office.

00:03:29.637 --> 00:03:31.723
- Is everything okay?
- Yeah. It's fine.

00:03:32.224 --> 00:03:33.892
I'm pregnant.

00:03:35.102 --> 00:03:36.646
Well, except for that.

00:04:12.649 --> 00:04:14.109
So it's official?

00:04:14.318 --> 00:04:16.195
Yeah. It is.

00:04:16.404 --> 00:04:18.406
And does she know who the father is?

00:04:18.615 --> 00:04:19.992
No.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:23.037
They don't like to do paternity
tests until the baby's born.

00:04:23.246 --> 00:04:25.165
Too dangerous, I guess.

00:04:25.373 --> 00:04:28.753
But there's a chance
that it could be yours?

00:04:33.801 --> 00:04:35.887
- We were broken up.
- Oh, right.

00:04:36.095 --> 00:04:38.098
No, totally.

00:04:40.267 --> 00:04:43.271
- We were broken up for, like, a week.
- I'm sorry.

00:04:43.479 --> 00:04:46.650
I wish I could take it back. Believe me.

00:04:49.821 --> 00:04:51.489
If you wanna...

00:04:51.698 --> 00:04:55.244
- You know, I'll understand.
- Like there's a choice.

00:04:55.453 --> 00:04:58.123
I mean, if you're the father, then...

00:04:59.166 --> 00:05:02.879
...well, you and Theresa...
- No. No, I want to help her out...

00:05:03.087 --> 00:05:04.714
...but I also...

00:05:04.923 --> 00:05:07.217
I want to make this work...

00:05:07.426 --> 00:05:09.428
...between us.

00:05:20.484 --> 00:05:22.278
These are decaf, right?
If they're not...

00:05:22.486 --> 00:05:25.073
...I'm gonna be up for days. Thank you.

00:05:25.615 --> 00:05:26.992
Thanks.

00:05:27.576 --> 00:05:29.746
- I'm freaking out, Cohen.
- You're freaking out?

00:05:29.954 --> 00:05:31.414
You hear about Ryan and Theresa?

00:05:31.581 --> 00:05:33.667
What about my best friend?

00:05:33.834 --> 00:05:36.671
- Princess Sparkle is freaking out?
- Marissa, dumb-ass.

00:05:36.879 --> 00:05:39.633
I always get those two confused.
They have really shiny hair.

00:05:39.841 --> 00:05:41.761
How can you even joke about this?

00:05:41.969 --> 00:05:43.680
Because, I don't know, I have to.

00:05:43.888 --> 00:05:46.558
I'm not emotionally equipped
to process this information.

00:05:46.725 --> 00:05:49.395
It's not bad enough she has to live
with Lucifer and Julie?

00:05:49.604 --> 00:05:53.066
- I get those two confused as well.
- What'll happen to Ryan and Marissa?

00:05:53.275 --> 00:05:54.944
They're, like, the perfect couple.

00:05:55.152 --> 00:05:57.906
Based on your parents' marriage,
I sort of understand that.

00:05:58.073 --> 00:06:01.660
- I'm holding hot coffee, Cohen.
- Look, I don't know what's gonna happen.

00:06:01.869 --> 00:06:04.372
I just wish there was something
I could do to help him.

00:06:04.581 --> 00:06:06.625
We just got past all this drama...

00:06:06.834 --> 00:06:08.961
...and this summer was supposed
to be all-time.

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:11.923
Yeah, well, now it's all up in the air.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:14.093
- We're not having sex, by the way.
- Excellent.

00:06:14.301 --> 00:06:16.429
There's not enough pain
and suffering already.

00:06:20.267 --> 00:06:21.644
Excuse me.

00:06:21.811 --> 00:06:23.897
Sorry about the wait.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:30.321
Hi.

00:06:31.114 --> 00:06:32.324
Hi.

00:06:32.532 --> 00:06:34.410
I wanted to see if you wanted to talk.

00:06:35.035 --> 00:06:37.455
We're a little understaffed.

00:06:37.664 --> 00:06:40.960
Eighty-five cents. Great. I'll put it
towards baby's college tuition.

00:06:41.168 --> 00:06:44.631
If you want to talk about it... That.

00:06:44.839 --> 00:06:46.842
Theresa, the register's broken.

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:49.011
Sorry.

00:07:13.625 --> 00:07:16.546
Now, there's a portrait of a man
headed to the altar.

00:07:16.713 --> 00:07:19.257
- What the hell do you want?
- No, it's not what I want.

00:07:19.466 --> 00:07:21.469
It's what Kirsten wants.

00:07:21.677 --> 00:07:23.513
D Átente. Peace.

00:07:23.721 --> 00:07:26.892
- The promise of a feud-free wedding.
- You've come to the wrong groom.

00:07:27.142 --> 00:07:29.270
You wanna apologize, do so,
but do it quick.

00:07:29.479 --> 00:07:32.149
You have no idea how much cajoling
it took to get me here.

00:07:32.315 --> 00:07:35.569
- I'm only here because of Kirsten.
- It's always because of Kirsten.

00:07:36.154 --> 00:07:38.156
When you railroaded my dinner...

00:07:38.365 --> 00:07:41.243
...was that because of her too?
- No, that one was for you.

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:44.414
So, what are you gonna do...

00:07:44.622 --> 00:07:46.834
...when I'm not around to make you
feel better about yourself?

00:07:47.042 --> 00:07:49.420
- You going somewhere?
- Maybe.

00:07:50.588 --> 00:07:52.549
Like, say, San Quentin.

00:07:55.302 --> 00:07:58.890
- What the hell are you talking about?
- What did you think I was doing in Vegas?

00:07:59.099 --> 00:08:01.185
Besides flipping my restaurant
for a tidy sum?

00:08:01.393 --> 00:08:03.271
I was trying to save the Newport Group.

00:08:03.479 --> 00:08:08.152
Selling that property was supposed to
keep this company from going bankrupt.

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:09.904
Kirsten never said anything.

00:08:10.071 --> 00:08:13.742
That's because residential real estate
is our only profitable division.

00:08:13.951 --> 00:08:18.081
She doesn't know anything about the
bad investments, the debts, the losses.

00:08:18.248 --> 00:08:21.627
Sell to somebody else. Robert Campbell
can't be the only buyer in town.

00:08:21.794 --> 00:08:25.507
It doesn't mean as much to anyone else.
Campbell owns the rest of the coastline.

00:08:25.715 --> 00:08:28.552
This property was the last piece
of the puzzle he was missing.

00:08:28.761 --> 00:08:31.514
So that's why you wanted us
out of the restaurant so fast.

00:08:31.681 --> 00:08:33.892
You sneaky...

00:08:34.101 --> 00:08:36.854
...not-so-successful son of a bitch.

00:08:37.021 --> 00:08:39.107
Enjoy it while you can.

00:08:39.316 --> 00:08:41.861
I got the DA all over me again.

00:08:42.069 --> 00:08:44.990
Must smell blood in the water.

00:08:45.156 --> 00:08:47.660
Have a nice day, Sandy.

00:08:56.254 --> 00:08:57.714
- Hey, kiddo.
- Hey.

00:08:58.381 --> 00:08:59.633
What are you doing?

00:08:59.841 --> 00:09:03.137
You know, preparing to move
into the house on Haunted Hill.

00:09:04.597 --> 00:09:06.266
You know...

00:09:06.475 --> 00:09:09.479
...you don't have to do this.
I'd sooner give back the check...

00:09:09.687 --> 00:09:13.025
...than have you move in with your mom.
- Then you're left with nothing.

00:09:13.233 --> 00:09:14.860
You'd have to move to Phoenix.

00:09:15.069 --> 00:09:18.073
Well, at least this way,
I can still see you.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:24.247
Life just wasn't this complicated
when I was growing up.

00:09:26.249 --> 00:09:30.296
Yeah, I know. It feels like we're
constantly being punished for something.

00:09:30.755 --> 00:09:32.591
- Mom just keeps on ticking.
- Hey.

00:09:32.799 --> 00:09:36.095
Your mom has to wake up every
morning and be Julie Cooper.

00:09:36.763 --> 00:09:39.057
That is punishment enough.

00:09:42.061 --> 00:09:44.022
Come on. Let's take a break.
What do you say?

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:46.400
Go down to the pier and get a Balboa Bar?

00:09:48.444 --> 00:09:49.737
I can't.

00:09:49.946 --> 00:09:52.240
I've just got so much to do.

00:09:59.332 --> 00:10:02.420
- Does Theresa's mom know?
- No, not yet.

00:10:02.587 --> 00:10:04.297
Theresa's not ready to tell her.

00:10:04.506 --> 00:10:06.216
Besides, it'll make it feel too real.

00:10:06.425 --> 00:10:08.302
I have news for you. It's real.

00:10:08.511 --> 00:10:11.055
- Sandy.
- There's no point in sugarcoating it.

00:10:11.264 --> 00:10:13.767
You know how many unwed mothers
come through my office?

00:10:13.976 --> 00:10:15.353
We all know how real this is.

00:10:15.519 --> 00:10:18.440
- Can we just eat dinner?
- All right.

00:10:19.858 --> 00:10:21.777
Hey, look...

00:10:21.986 --> 00:10:24.614
...we are what we are,
and we'll help you through this.

00:10:25.198 --> 00:10:26.742
- We can do it together.
- Hey, man.

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:29.203
They raised me, okay? Proof pudding.

00:10:29.704 --> 00:10:32.374
Speaking of pudding, Mother,
do I have any tapioca on tap?

00:10:32.582 --> 00:10:35.795
- You are king of the segue.
- I just love pudding. It's so fun to say.

00:10:36.003 --> 00:10:38.465
Pudding. Pudding.

00:10:38.673 --> 00:10:40.926
Our child-rearing skills speak
for themselves.

00:10:41.135 --> 00:10:42.511
Pudding.

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:43.972
Oh, hi, sweetie.

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:46.308
I have my secret recipe, takeout.

00:10:46.516 --> 00:10:48.185
- No, thanks. I ate at work.
- Pudding.

00:10:48.394 --> 00:10:52.065
- Ryan, can we talk?
- Yeah. Yeah, sure.

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:03.454
So, what's going on?

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:05.874
I've been thinking.

00:11:06.875 --> 00:11:09.378
We haven't really talked about it.

00:11:12.132 --> 00:11:14.552
You're not ready for this.

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:18.473
- I'm not ready for this.
- Yeah, I know, but we can...

00:11:18.682 --> 00:11:20.434
I can't do this.

00:11:21.101 --> 00:11:23.187
I'm not gonna do it.

00:11:24.481 --> 00:11:26.608
I'm not gonna have it.

00:11:26.817 --> 00:11:28.986
The baby.

00:11:32.032 --> 00:11:33.617
You're not?

00:11:36.078 --> 00:11:38.164
You can tell the Cohens...

00:11:38.373 --> 00:11:40.000
...but I can't tell my mom.

00:11:44.214 --> 00:11:46.508
Hey, you're off the hook.

00:11:58.315 --> 00:12:01.235
I have to go down and renew
my dock fees for my boat, man.

00:12:01.443 --> 00:12:04.447
You wanna go down there with me,
maybe take her out for a spin?

00:12:04.614 --> 00:12:06.575
- Sure, sounds good.
- No, it sounds great.

00:12:06.783 --> 00:12:09.078
Come on. We haven't even been on
since last summer.

00:12:09.287 --> 00:12:12.123
Remember last summer? We were
just getting to know each other.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.835
Now look at us. Best friends.
Brothers, even.

00:12:15.044 --> 00:12:17.463
What do brothers do, Ryan?
You know what brothers do?

00:12:17.672 --> 00:12:19.675
Brothers sail.

00:12:19.883 --> 00:12:21.594
What brothers sail?

00:12:21.802 --> 00:12:24.639
The Wright Brothers.
Before they invented airplanes.

00:12:24.848 --> 00:12:26.516
How do you think they got everywhere?

00:12:26.725 --> 00:12:28.352
The Ringling Brothers...

00:12:28.561 --> 00:12:32.649
...with their chimps and their tigers.
It was like Noah's Ark on that boat.

00:12:32.858 --> 00:12:35.695
- Hanson. Playing cruise lines.
- Okay, we'll go sailing.

00:12:35.861 --> 00:12:39.533
No, get excited, okay?
You dodged a bullet.

00:12:40.159 --> 00:12:42.662
Not that... Not that... It's... You...

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:44.622
Bullet.

00:12:44.831 --> 00:12:46.500
I just think that it's cool.

00:12:46.708 --> 00:12:48.002
Not so much cool, but...

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:50.880
Okay, I just... I don't know.
I thought you'd be relieved.

00:12:51.047 --> 00:12:53.592
No. No, I am. It's complicated.

00:12:53.801 --> 00:12:56.804
Too complicated for banter
about boats and Hanson?

00:13:03.479 --> 00:13:05.482
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:09.153
Can I get you anything?
Tea? Toast? Dramamine?

00:13:09.362 --> 00:13:10.822
No, thanks.

00:13:10.989 --> 00:13:13.742
I don't want to be late.
I'm only working a half-day today.

00:13:14.159 --> 00:13:16.120
I have an appointment
at Planned Parenthood.

00:13:16.621 --> 00:13:18.790
Is Ryan gonna go with you?

00:13:18.999 --> 00:13:22.211
No, I haven't told him.
He's freaked out enough as it is.

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:24.631
What about your mother?

00:13:24.839 --> 00:13:26.800
No, I can't.

00:13:27.009 --> 00:13:28.636
She's extremely religious.

00:13:30.138 --> 00:13:33.392
Well, you'll need someone there
to listen to the doctors...

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:36.354
...because you're gonna have
a million things on your mind.

00:13:36.896 --> 00:13:38.356
You won't want to drive.

00:13:38.565 --> 00:13:41.318
I'm an excellent driver
and amazing parker.

00:13:43.071 --> 00:13:45.907
Thanks. I hate parallel parking.

00:13:47.493 --> 00:13:49.120
So how are you doing with it?

00:13:49.328 --> 00:13:54.752
- Are you relieved, sad, disappointed?
- All of the above. Yes.

00:13:54.919 --> 00:13:58.340
- Well, did she say when she was gonna...?
- Soon.

00:13:59.174 --> 00:14:00.884
I guess.

00:14:02.678 --> 00:14:05.766
Well, then at least maybe everything
can go back to normal.

00:14:05.932 --> 00:14:08.769
Not that anything around here
ever is normal.

00:14:08.936 --> 00:14:11.231
More normal than this.

00:14:14.902 --> 00:14:19.366
I think we should spend this whole
summer just being normal.

00:14:19.574 --> 00:14:24.456
- We won't hold Seth to that, will we?
- No. No, that would be impossible.

00:14:25.665 --> 00:14:28.210
I was talking more about us.

00:14:37.722 --> 00:14:40.559
You're just full of surprises.

00:14:44.481 --> 00:14:46.859
I hear water. And by the way, Caleb...

00:14:47.067 --> 00:14:49.821
...we should hold on to this blindfold.

00:14:50.029 --> 00:14:52.741
- Oh, gosh.
- Good to know.

00:14:55.703 --> 00:14:58.456
Oh, my God! It's a palace.

00:14:58.665 --> 00:15:00.125
Fit for a queen?

00:15:00.584 --> 00:15:02.795
Oh, Cal. It's amazing.

00:15:03.004 --> 00:15:04.380
I built it just for you.

00:15:05.966 --> 00:15:09.220
It's more than I ever
could have imagined.

00:15:12.432 --> 00:15:14.810
I want to live here forever.

00:15:17.313 --> 00:15:19.983
Oh, I've missed you.

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:21.694
It's been too long.

00:15:21.861 --> 00:15:24.906
- You're talking to a boat, Seth.
- I talk to a plastic horse too...

00:15:25.115 --> 00:15:27.409
...but that never worries anyone.
- It worried me.

00:15:27.618 --> 00:15:29.328
Hey.

00:15:29.704 --> 00:15:31.498
I forgot about this.

00:15:31.706 --> 00:15:34.043
This compass is gonna lead me
all the way to Tahiti.

00:15:34.251 --> 00:15:37.797
Yeah, whatever happened to that
big plan to sail to Tahiti?

00:15:38.006 --> 00:15:39.800
You showed up, man.

00:15:40.008 --> 00:15:41.844
Suddenly, I had much less reason to flee.

00:15:43.221 --> 00:15:45.974
Newport became kind of...

00:15:46.683 --> 00:15:48.769
- Kind of all right.
- Yeah?

00:15:49.562 --> 00:15:52.399
- Could've done it in 42 days, though.
- Guess we'll never know.

00:15:52.566 --> 00:15:54.693
Yeah, but now that we've got...

00:15:54.902 --> 00:15:57.781
...the Summer Breeze back in action,
we can sail to Catalina.

00:15:57.947 --> 00:15:59.574
We can take our ladies.

00:15:59.783 --> 00:16:01.952
Catch fresh fish right off
the side of the boat.

00:16:02.161 --> 00:16:04.497
Cook them right there.
Sounds good, man.

00:16:07.251 --> 00:16:09.545
Sounds great.

00:16:12.883 --> 00:16:15.636
So I'll take you
to your appointment tomorrow.

00:16:15.803 --> 00:16:19.516
You're not taking any anesthetics, so you
don't have to worry about what to eat.

00:16:19.725 --> 00:16:21.852
We'll get there about
a half an hour before...

00:16:22.061 --> 00:16:23.521
...and fill out some forms.

00:16:24.189 --> 00:16:26.859
Everyone there seems really nice.

00:16:27.568 --> 00:16:30.405
I can't believe I'm actually doing this.

00:16:31.364 --> 00:16:33.283
You don't have to.

00:16:33.826 --> 00:16:36.162
Yeah, I do. I mean...

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:39.166
...I'm in high school, or I should be.

00:16:39.416 --> 00:16:41.710
I make $ 11 a day in tips.

00:16:42.837 --> 00:16:45.173
Not having this baby...

00:16:45.382 --> 00:16:48.052
...makes the most sense.

00:16:50.471 --> 00:16:53.517
You don't have to make the decision
that makes the most sense.

00:16:53.725 --> 00:16:57.564
Right. Coming from you... I mean...

00:16:57.772 --> 00:16:59.232
...your life is so together.

00:16:59.399 --> 00:17:02.403
You know, you have
an amazing family...

00:17:02.570 --> 00:17:04.030
...great job.

00:17:04.239 --> 00:17:05.532
It's perfect.

00:17:07.117 --> 00:17:09.203
Nothing's perfect.

00:17:11.581 --> 00:17:13.375
Sometimes...

00:17:14.585 --> 00:17:18.214
...things just happen.

00:17:18.423 --> 00:17:21.594
Yeah, but never to someone
like you, right?

00:17:28.519 --> 00:17:30.355
- I'm sorry. L...
- It's okay.

00:17:30.563 --> 00:17:32.816
I don't regret the decision I made.

00:17:35.152 --> 00:17:39.533
I just wish that when I was
trying to choose...

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:42.787
...there was someone there for me.

00:17:44.247 --> 00:17:46.750
Whatever you decide...

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:49.295
...we're here for you.

00:18:03.396 --> 00:18:04.856
Hi.

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:11.823
How you feeling?

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:13.909
Pretty lousy.

00:18:16.913 --> 00:18:21.293
Remember that part last night
about me not having the baby?

00:18:22.545 --> 00:18:24.965
As hard as it is to imagine
having a baby...

00:18:25.173 --> 00:18:28.886
...I can't really imagine not having it.

00:18:33.433 --> 00:18:35.645
So you're gonna have it.

00:18:35.853 --> 00:18:38.023
I have to.

00:18:48.411 --> 00:18:49.871
Well, what did you say to her?

00:18:50.079 --> 00:18:51.331
I didn't say anything.

00:18:51.539 --> 00:18:54.293
So all of a sudden she just decided
to change her mind?

00:18:54.501 --> 00:18:57.589
No, it's all of a sudden that
she made all of her decisions.

00:18:57.797 --> 00:19:00.634
What? You talked her
into having this child.

00:19:00.801 --> 00:19:03.388
So I should let her make
a totally uninformed decision?

00:19:03.596 --> 00:19:06.099
They're kids with nothing.
How can they start a family?

00:19:06.308 --> 00:19:08.018
That's not our choice.

00:19:08.227 --> 00:19:09.854
You know what Ryan's going through?

00:19:10.021 --> 00:19:12.858
Not as well as I know
what she's going through.

00:19:14.777 --> 00:19:16.154
What does that mean?

00:19:16.571 --> 00:19:17.739
Nothing.

00:19:17.947 --> 00:19:21.619
It's just, she's alone. She can't talk to
her mother. She's scared and confused.

00:19:21.827 --> 00:19:23.830
All I did was listen.

00:19:24.664 --> 00:19:28.002
- Oh, hey. You want some breakfast?
- No, thanks. I'll get something later.

00:19:28.169 --> 00:19:30.713
I just want to see if Theresa
wants anything.

00:19:32.132 --> 00:19:34.259
I should call my dad.
He has to be here by 8.

00:19:34.468 --> 00:19:36.596
Have you talked to him?
He doesn't seem himself.

00:19:36.804 --> 00:19:39.808
I can't blame him.
I wouldn't want to be him either.

00:19:39.975 --> 00:19:42.061
He's about to be bound by law
to Julie Cooper.

00:19:42.270 --> 00:19:46.108
Don't remind me. Denial is a
very effective coping mechanism.

00:19:46.316 --> 00:19:47.568
It should be some weekend.

00:19:48.027 --> 00:19:49.821
Hi.

00:19:49.987 --> 00:19:52.908
Want some breakfast? Pancakes?
Waffles?

00:19:54.910 --> 00:19:57.914
- You're leaving.
- I'm going home.

00:19:58.081 --> 00:19:59.332
I talked to my mom.

00:19:59.541 --> 00:20:01.335
I told her everything.

00:20:02.253 --> 00:20:05.340
I should have left last night
when I saw the look on your face.

00:20:07.843 --> 00:20:09.720
You don't have to leave.

00:20:11.264 --> 00:20:13.517
We can figure this out together.

00:20:18.857 --> 00:20:21.068
Then come with me.

00:20:27.618 --> 00:20:31.665
Never mind breakfast.
I'll grab something on the road.

00:20:37.881 --> 00:20:39.508
This place is huge.

00:20:39.716 --> 00:20:40.968
It's a castle.

00:20:41.176 --> 00:20:43.930
The torture chamber must be
in the basement.

00:20:45.223 --> 00:20:46.850
Jimmy, what...?

00:20:47.059 --> 00:20:50.313
You should not be here. Caleb's due
back any minute, and thanks to you...

00:20:50.521 --> 00:20:52.983
...he has to take his wedding photos
with a black eye.

00:20:53.191 --> 00:20:56.195
It'll match the black lump of coal
where his heart should be.

00:20:56.404 --> 00:20:58.573
Why can't you be happy for me? I am.

00:20:58.782 --> 00:21:01.368
Julie, you can't be happy.

00:21:01.577 --> 00:21:04.873
- And that makes me happy.
- Classy choice, Jimmy.

00:21:05.081 --> 00:21:08.669
Although, it's obvious you're with her
because you can't be with Kirsten.

00:21:08.878 --> 00:21:11.381
I think, in psychology,
that's called "transference."

00:21:11.965 --> 00:21:14.218
And you marrying Caleb,
I think, in psychology...

00:21:14.426 --> 00:21:16.596
...that's called "shameless gold-digging."
- No.

00:21:16.804 --> 00:21:19.474
- That's what his youngest daughter's for.
- Don't make me...

00:21:19.641 --> 00:21:22.562
Make you what? Go back to life
as a stripper or a coke whore?

00:21:23.312 --> 00:21:26.233
- Someone forgotten about the '80s?
- At least I'm not a criminal.

00:21:26.441 --> 00:21:29.111
- Yeah, you're just marrying one.
- Okay, stop it.

00:21:29.320 --> 00:21:33.158
Just stop it. No more fighting, okay?

00:21:33.367 --> 00:21:36.996
Look, you're getting what you wanted.
I'm moving in with you.

00:21:38.415 --> 00:21:41.752
Well, that's what you wanted too,
right, sweetie?

00:21:48.552 --> 00:21:50.179
I've got some more stuff in the car.

00:21:50.388 --> 00:21:53.141
I'll get the rest of my stuff
out of your house tomorrow.

00:21:57.730 --> 00:22:00.818
I can't believe your boat's name
is Summer. What a coincidence.

00:22:00.985 --> 00:22:03.738
My name's Summer.
Your boat's named Summer.

00:22:03.905 --> 00:22:07.242
- It's kind of crazy.
- Yeah, it's just crazy.

00:22:07.451 --> 00:22:09.996
Well, it's the only Summer
you'll be riding for a while.

00:22:10.204 --> 00:22:12.457
Right. Yeah, no sex. I got it. Thank you.

00:22:12.666 --> 00:22:15.086
- Hey, Seth.
- Hey.

00:22:15.252 --> 00:22:17.839
- You got that paperwork?
- Yeah.

00:22:22.011 --> 00:22:24.097
So it's still in really good condition.

00:22:24.305 --> 00:22:27.559
I got a guy, I think he'll offer 6000.
He's been bugging me a while.

00:22:27.768 --> 00:22:29.729
Great. Will you remember to get cash?

00:22:29.896 --> 00:22:31.272
- I told him.
- All right. Thanks.

00:22:31.481 --> 00:22:33.191
- Come by tomorrow.
- I will.

00:22:33.567 --> 00:22:35.361
Six thousand dollars in cash?

00:22:35.569 --> 00:22:38.239
- Are you fleeing the country, Cohen?
- No, it's for Ryan.

00:22:38.406 --> 00:22:39.866
What? For vintage wife-beaters?

00:22:42.286 --> 00:22:44.664
It's actually for Theresa.

00:22:44.873 --> 00:22:46.667
For Ryan to give to Theresa.

00:22:48.043 --> 00:22:52.424
Listen, don't say anything, okay? Because
I don't even think Ryan's told Marissa yet.

00:22:52.632 --> 00:22:54.301
But...

00:22:54.510 --> 00:22:56.387
...I think Theresa's gonna have her baby.

00:22:56.596 --> 00:22:58.056
What?

00:22:58.640 --> 00:22:59.933
- Oh, my God.
- I know.

00:23:00.559 --> 00:23:04.314
And she's gonna need money, and, you
know, I spent all mine on Vegas hookers.

00:23:04.522 --> 00:23:07.276
So this is the only thing
I have that's worth anything.

00:23:08.194 --> 00:23:09.904
I just don't know how else to help.

00:23:11.072 --> 00:23:12.783
Cohen...

00:23:23.671 --> 00:23:25.882
- What the hell's he doing here?
- He's family too.

00:23:26.091 --> 00:23:27.885
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:23:28.052 --> 00:23:29.971
- How you doing, Caleb?
- Get away from me.

00:23:30.179 --> 00:23:31.723
- Dad.
- Well...

00:23:31.932 --> 00:23:35.686
...congrats. She's a hell of a woman.

00:23:37.814 --> 00:23:40.359
- Congratulations, Mrs. Cooper.
- Oh, thank you.

00:23:40.567 --> 00:23:43.905
Seth. You excited
about being a groomsman?

00:23:44.823 --> 00:23:47.910
It's the fulfillment
of a lifelong dream, yeah.

00:23:48.869 --> 00:23:50.663
- Hey, guys.
- Marissa.

00:23:50.872 --> 00:23:54.084
- You look beautiful.
- Thanks.

00:23:58.924 --> 00:24:02.011
Hey, have you guys seen Ryan?
He didn't call me back earlier.

00:24:02.178 --> 00:24:03.554
- Do you think he's okay?
- Yeah.

00:24:03.763 --> 00:24:06.266
- He takes a long time with his hair.
- His hair, yeah.

00:24:06.433 --> 00:24:10.563
- Bangs. I don't know. Mousse. Product.
- You should see him. It's weird.

00:24:11.439 --> 00:24:13.066
So, Cal...

00:24:14.401 --> 00:24:16.529
...I talked to the DA.

00:24:16.738 --> 00:24:19.074
- Otis?
- Yeah.

00:24:19.533 --> 00:24:21.702
What did that pantload have
to say for himself?

00:24:21.911 --> 00:24:23.538
It's over.

00:24:26.208 --> 00:24:28.502
What the hell am I supposed to do?

00:24:29.796 --> 00:24:33.175
Well, have you told the future Mrs. Nichol
about your financial situation?

00:24:33.383 --> 00:24:34.927
What are you saying, Sandy?

00:24:35.094 --> 00:24:37.055
That Julie's only marrying me
for my money?

00:24:37.222 --> 00:24:38.932
No, never.

00:24:39.099 --> 00:24:41.101
Course not.
But you might think...

00:24:41.310 --> 00:24:43.396
...about postponing this thing.
- Impossible.

00:24:43.605 --> 00:24:45.649
The wedding is tomorrow.

00:24:45.857 --> 00:24:50.154
I have never let anyone push me around,
and this is no exception.

00:24:50.488 --> 00:24:52.574
But thanks...

00:24:52.783 --> 00:24:54.243
...for trying.

00:24:54.410 --> 00:24:56.245
I appreciate it.

00:24:57.163 --> 00:24:59.291
It's ironic.

00:24:59.541 --> 00:25:02.295
Julie leaves Jimmy, marries you.
Now he's worth millions...

00:25:02.920 --> 00:25:05.215
...and you're gonna be broke.

00:25:05.423 --> 00:25:06.675
I don't believe in irony.

00:25:06.884 --> 00:25:09.053
Well, that's too bad...

00:25:09.262 --> 00:25:12.265
...because it might be just the thing
to get you through this.

00:25:16.729 --> 00:25:19.816
Hey. What are you doing?

00:25:20.025 --> 00:25:21.318
I'm just...

00:25:21.527 --> 00:25:23.488
...you know, hiding.

00:25:23.696 --> 00:25:26.450
Yeah. I can't blame you.

00:25:26.658 --> 00:25:30.413
- So where's Theresa?
- She went back home.

00:25:30.622 --> 00:25:32.499
To have the baby.

00:25:34.418 --> 00:25:37.422
Well, did she and Eddie make up?

00:25:40.801 --> 00:25:43.680
So she's having the baby alone.

00:25:52.566 --> 00:25:55.319
I'll keep it brief, I promise.

00:25:55.945 --> 00:25:59.533
First, I'd like to thank Kirsten
for hosting a wonderful dinner...

00:25:59.741 --> 00:26:01.368
...and to say...

00:26:01.577 --> 00:26:05.040
...tomorrow is a truly important event.

00:26:05.791 --> 00:26:10.547
As a father, it's a great joy to have
a family and to watch that family grow.

00:26:11.548 --> 00:26:14.134
We've all been through
a great deal together...

00:26:14.343 --> 00:26:16.137
...for better and for worse.

00:26:16.304 --> 00:26:17.555
But tomorrow...

00:26:18.181 --> 00:26:22.687
...the Nichols, the Cohens
and the Coopers become one family.

00:26:23.646 --> 00:26:27.192
And I feel very lucky to be
at the head of that family.

00:26:27.401 --> 00:26:30.238
Cheers and many thanks.

00:26:31.406 --> 00:26:33.116
Cheers.

00:26:44.255 --> 00:26:47.009
Hey, are you okay?

00:26:47.217 --> 00:26:49.554
I just need some air.

00:26:50.930 --> 00:26:52.140
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:26:52.349 --> 00:26:54.518
Everything okay?

00:26:54.977 --> 00:26:57.397
- Can we just get out of here?
- Please.

00:27:01.443 --> 00:27:03.571
You know, Ryan, I...

00:27:03.780 --> 00:27:05.741
I think it was this very stretch
of beach...

00:27:05.949 --> 00:27:08.869
...where we first got our asses kicked
by the water-polo team.

00:27:09.036 --> 00:27:10.288
Yeah?

00:27:10.496 --> 00:27:12.123
Could be.

00:27:14.460 --> 00:27:17.046
Yes, it definitely tastes the same.

00:27:17.547 --> 00:27:19.925
Wait, when was that?

00:27:20.134 --> 00:27:23.304
- When I first got here.
- Yeah, it was after that fashion show...

00:27:23.513 --> 00:27:24.889
...at Holly's beach house.

00:27:25.056 --> 00:27:27.059
You guys were at that party?

00:27:28.644 --> 00:27:30.814
Those were the days.

00:27:33.942 --> 00:27:35.236
Hey...

00:27:35.444 --> 00:27:37.405
...you feeling better?

00:27:41.118 --> 00:27:42.995
I've been thinking.

00:27:45.791 --> 00:27:47.668
I think...

00:27:49.629 --> 00:27:51.715
...I need to go back.

00:27:54.635 --> 00:27:57.639
I can't let Theresa do this by herself.

00:28:07.276 --> 00:28:09.570
I'm leaving.

00:28:20.459 --> 00:28:21.919
Hey.

00:28:22.128 --> 00:28:24.339
So we all good? Proof of purchase?
Bill of sale?

00:28:24.798 --> 00:28:27.343
Yeah, so the guy called me
this morning, said he...

00:28:27.593 --> 00:28:29.971
...couldn't come up with the money.
- What?

00:28:30.179 --> 00:28:32.599
What the hell, man?
You told me it was a done deal.

00:28:32.808 --> 00:28:37.438
- He said give him a couple of months.
- I can't do that. I need it right now.

00:28:37.981 --> 00:28:41.569
- Just forget it. It just figures...
- Sorry, man.

00:28:41.777 --> 00:28:43.154
Yeah, well...

00:28:43.321 --> 00:28:46.074
...that's the way it's been
going for me lately.

00:28:52.457 --> 00:28:54.960
Hey. Okay, I have a plan.

00:28:55.169 --> 00:28:57.756
Listen, Ryan doesn't want
to leave, right?

00:28:57.964 --> 00:29:00.175
We don't want him to leave. So...

00:29:00.384 --> 00:29:01.677
...let's not let him.

00:29:01.886 --> 00:29:05.265
We can all get jobs. We can pool
our salaries and cover his apartment...

00:29:05.474 --> 00:29:07.434
...an apartment up
in the numbered streets.

00:29:07.643 --> 00:29:10.897
Except Theresa wants to be with
her family, and Ryan has to be with her.

00:29:11.106 --> 00:29:13.191
What? You wanna give up?
You wanna let him go?

00:29:13.400 --> 00:29:17.363
Look, there's nothing else we can do,
other than kidnap him.

00:29:19.616 --> 00:29:21.577
If there was something I could do,
I would.

00:29:21.786 --> 00:29:23.579
Well, I think you've
done enough, so...

00:29:23.788 --> 00:29:25.916
- What does that mean?
- I don't think Ryan...

00:29:26.124 --> 00:29:28.961
...would be back with Theresa
if it wasn't for you and Oliver.

00:29:29.128 --> 00:29:30.338
- Cohen.
- Really...

00:29:30.547 --> 00:29:34.259
...all you ever did was drag that kid
into your messed-up life. I just...

00:29:34.468 --> 00:29:37.138
Right. You used him to meet girls
and get out of fights.

00:29:37.347 --> 00:29:40.225
- Okay, you guys, come on.
- I don't really care.

00:29:40.392 --> 00:29:43.897
I've gotta get ready. So as long
as you're cool with him leaving...

00:29:47.860 --> 00:29:50.029
- Hey.
- Hi.

00:29:50.238 --> 00:29:53.367
We'll probably leave in an hour
if Kirsten can get ready in time.

00:29:53.575 --> 00:29:55.703
It is a mystery what goes on
in that bathroom.

00:29:55.912 --> 00:29:58.206
- Think you'll be done by 6?
- God, I hope so.

00:29:59.708 --> 00:30:02.461
That's what time I told Theresa
to pick me up.

00:30:05.590 --> 00:30:08.010
You know, as your guardian...

00:30:08.844 --> 00:30:10.555
...I can stop you.

00:30:12.432 --> 00:30:14.685
But if you taught me anything...

00:30:15.060 --> 00:30:18.440
...you gotta do whatever it takes
to protect your family.

00:30:19.691 --> 00:30:23.029
- She's my family now.
- We are too.

00:30:23.780 --> 00:30:29.036
You can stay here. So can she.
We can make this work as a family.

00:30:29.704 --> 00:30:31.790
I can't.

00:30:32.749 --> 00:30:35.086
I can't ask that of you.

00:30:35.920 --> 00:30:37.756
You've done more than enough...

00:30:37.964 --> 00:30:40.509
...more than I ever could've asked
of anyone.

00:30:40.718 --> 00:30:42.595
I told you...

00:30:43.596 --> 00:30:46.350
...you could've done worse.
- No.

00:30:47.309 --> 00:30:49.437
When you took me in, I had nothing.

00:30:49.645 --> 00:30:52.816
No family, no hope.

00:30:56.529 --> 00:30:59.783
I don't want this kid
to grow up like I did.

00:31:05.332 --> 00:31:07.042
Well...

00:31:07.918 --> 00:31:10.338
...just because you're leaving...

00:31:10.839 --> 00:31:13.592
...doesn't mean I'm letting you go.

00:31:17.680 --> 00:31:20.058
Now, come on, get dressed.

00:31:20.267 --> 00:31:23.605
We gotta witness the most
unholy of all unions.

00:33:26.800 --> 00:33:28.928
You want to dance?

00:33:52.207 --> 00:33:54.960
I just want you to know...

00:33:55.920 --> 00:33:58.757
...I understand why you have to do this.

00:34:04.431 --> 00:34:06.058
Thanks.

00:34:08.686 --> 00:34:11.189
But I wish you didn't have to.

00:34:11.398 --> 00:34:13.275
Me too.

00:34:24.080 --> 00:34:26.166
I love you.

00:35:27.451 --> 00:35:29.370
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:35:29.579 --> 00:35:31.748
They sent me out to find you.

00:35:32.833 --> 00:35:34.919
Found you.

00:35:36.212 --> 00:35:39.925
I figured you'd be stuffing your pockets
with cocktail weenies.

00:35:43.596 --> 00:35:45.682
You're still gonna see him.

00:35:45.891 --> 00:35:47.685
Chino's not that far away.

00:35:47.851 --> 00:35:50.146
I just can't believe he's leaving.

00:35:50.355 --> 00:35:53.025
He's the first real friend I've ever had.

00:35:53.817 --> 00:35:56.487
He's the only real friend I've ever had.

00:35:57.322 --> 00:35:58.782
I know.

00:36:00.534 --> 00:36:04.831
- You have me.
- Yeah, but that's not the same thing.

00:36:05.040 --> 00:36:07.209
You don't get it. Before he got here...

00:36:07.376 --> 00:36:11.297
...I was the biggest loser.
This place was hell for me, okay?

00:36:13.509 --> 00:36:15.803
And I can't help him, and...
I can't even imagine...

00:36:16.012 --> 00:36:18.557
...what it's gonna be like
here without him.

00:36:21.685 --> 00:36:25.482
We'll make it through it. I promise.

00:36:27.359 --> 00:36:30.822
Could you tell them that I'll be back
in a few minutes, please?

00:36:31.030 --> 00:36:32.240
Sure.

00:36:35.536 --> 00:36:37.580
Yeah, for the record...

00:36:40.334 --> 00:36:43.171
...the boat was named after you.

00:37:13.709 --> 00:37:14.960
Hey.

00:37:15.169 --> 00:37:17.297
- Hi.
- Is Theresa here?

00:37:18.340 --> 00:37:20.134
Should be soon.

00:37:21.469 --> 00:37:23.513
A little something for the road.

00:37:24.180 --> 00:37:27.101
Don't worry, I didn't make it.

00:37:27.309 --> 00:37:29.270
But if I did learn to cook...

00:37:29.520 --> 00:37:32.023
...could we convince you to stay?

00:37:38.073 --> 00:37:40.909
Thank you for...

00:37:41.076 --> 00:37:43.037
...inviting me into your home.

00:37:44.706 --> 00:37:46.959
You guys...

00:37:48.043 --> 00:37:50.463
This year was...

00:37:50.672 --> 00:37:52.674
For us too.

00:38:11.448 --> 00:38:13.951
And Kirsten's not even a hugger.

00:38:15.494 --> 00:38:17.831
You always know how to ruin a moment.

00:38:18.039 --> 00:38:20.125
That's what I do.

00:38:21.752 --> 00:38:23.922
I'm gonna say goodbye to Seth.

00:38:29.804 --> 00:38:32.808
- Hey, man.
- Hi.

00:38:34.476 --> 00:38:35.853
Gotta jet.

00:38:36.062 --> 00:38:37.313
Cool.

00:38:39.191 --> 00:38:41.360
You really gotta go?

00:38:41.944 --> 00:38:43.571
Yeah.

00:38:44.531 --> 00:38:47.743
Well, if you need a nanny,
I'll take the graveyard shift.

00:38:47.952 --> 00:38:50.288
I think we'll manage.

00:38:50.955 --> 00:38:53.333
I was afraid you'd say that.

00:38:56.421 --> 00:38:58.798
You can come down and visit me.

00:39:05.724 --> 00:39:08.144
Hey, so I...

00:39:08.352 --> 00:39:10.647
I got you something.

00:39:12.315 --> 00:39:14.026
It's yours, you know.

00:39:14.193 --> 00:39:17.030
- Always good for ideas.
- Map of Tahiti.

00:39:17.196 --> 00:39:19.199
Cool, man.

00:39:29.170 --> 00:39:30.880
So I'll see you, then.

00:39:31.047 --> 00:39:32.924
See you.
